                <pb facs="0758" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/409: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Luxemburg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Waller</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Luxemburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-27T12:00:00+01:00">June 27,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 27—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. I have strongest reason to believe that the Grand Ducal Government, having a
                    refugee problem of its own and lying on German frontier, desirous of cooperating
                    in refugee questions, would welcome an invitation to be represented at meeting
                    at Evian on July 6. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Waller</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
